\section*{The sharp singularity exponent of biased symmetric sign matrices}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. With fixed sign bias $p\ne1/2$, the claimed symmetric-matrix singularity rate is $(p^2+(1-p)^2+o(1))^n$, attained by equal rows.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Kernel vectors determine possible exposed columns, with sparse-tail cases separated from the conditioned bit model. Lattice tools and prime-field corank bounds control the structured alternatives; the biased column estimate matches the repeated-row lower rate.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
